json/key
description: Double-quoted string naming the value
- >
  A key is a double-quoted string - lexically the same as
  [json/string](::language:concretes:07-json_code:01-json_scalar:00-json_string), but its role
  differs: it names a value rather than being data itself. The quotes are mandatory - `age` bare or
  `42` are not valid JSON keys, while `"age"` and `"42"` are:
- !!<format: text/x-json> |
  "age"
